  "body": "Stacked on #3130 (merge #3130 first).\n\n## Final validation\n\n- Head: `1d1fd8b7204f05e3e69d46dce55922d2ec5a172b`.\n- Tested base: `upstream/main` at `60cb97a0b3717bf6a129e781fd8f4ec98806124b`.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 735 steps pass, with zero failures, in 48.5 minutes.\n- Five focused motion suites: 97 tests pass. The requested `center_cut_law`, `level_links`, and `machining2d` suites pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN. All 235 steps pass in 37.4 minutes. The reached motion and app lanes pass.\n- Heavy totals: 100 ordinary tests pass. No ordinary test fails or is ignored. The gate also accepts six expected failures.\n- Heavy steps: one release build, 35 motion targets, 193 app targets, and six known-fail checks.\n- `cargo clippy -j4 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN, in 1 minute 25 seconds.\n\nReview mutation checks:\n\n- Disable the prior-feed check: the focused crossing pin fails. The broad pin reports the original six crossing pairs. Restore: all seven `center_cut_law` tests pass.\n- Remove the closing rings: the square pin fails (two dives against four). The island pin fails (ten against fourteen).\n- Force an infinite stay-down distance: the KeepDown pin fails.\n- Restore the count and link mutations: all 80 tests in `machining2d` and `level_links` pass. The final tree is clean.\n\nReached heavy lanes with ordinary tests:\n\n| Lane | Target | Passed |\n|---|---|---:|\n| motion | `lib` | 8 |\n| motion | `adaptive_hsm` | 5 |\n| motion | `adaptive_troch_neck` | 1 |\n| motion | `finish3d` | 33 |\n| motion | `finish3d_gaplink` | 1 |\n| motion | `flow` | 2 |\n| motion | `lead_room` | 1 |\n| motion | `offset_shells` | 1 |\n| motion | `pivot5d` | 1 |\n| motion | `pocket3d_hsm` | 1 |\n| motion | `rotary_adaptive` | 3 |\n| app | `adaptive_fig8_crossing` | 2 |\n| app | `adaptive_pinch` | 1 |\n| app | `carried_engine_agreement` | 1 |\n| app | `example_catalog` | 2 |\n| app | `feature_pick_wire` | 1 |\n| app | `import_solidcraft` | 3 |\n| app | `large_models` | 1 |\n| app | `lathe_field_sim` | 1 |\n| app | `lathe_workholding_kinds` | 1 |\n| app | `operations` | 6 |\n| app | `pick_agnostic` | 2 |\n| app | `pocket3d_hsm` | 1 |\n| app | `rotary_field_parity` | 6 |\n| app | `shared_face_bodies_finish` | 6 |\n| app | `shoulder_adaptive` | 1 |\n| app | `stock_engine_agreement` | 3 |\n| app | `stock_field_cost` | 1 |\n| app | `stock_play_precalc` | 1 |\n| app | `verify` | 2 |\n| app | `whole_model_pocket` | 1 |\n\nThe other 24 motion targets and 173 app targets select no ordinary ignored test.\nKnown-fail checks remain separate from the 100 passing tests. Issue #1950 has two motion checks and one app check. Issue #2849 has three app checks. All six fail at their expected assertions, and the gate accepts them.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `pocket_avoid` (2D pocket with \"Do not touch\"): Zigzag and Auto levels now use `pocket_zigzag::rest_passes`. The rows stand 0.01 mm inside the level area. Then one closed ring follows each boundary loop: the wall, each island, and each keep-out edge.\n- `machining3d::hsm::plan_level` (3D pocket levels, strategy Zigzag or Auto): the same plan.\n- The rotary wrap (Rotary Offset) also reads `plan_level`, always with a seam. It keeps its rows. Its developed area ends at the seam, and a ring there cuts one seam line two times.\n- `rest_passes` is now `pub(crate)`. `machining2d` re-exports it as `zigzag_ringed_passes` for `machining3d`.\n\n## Cause\n\nA Zigzag row touches a wall or an island only at its ends. A cusp stays between each two ends over the full depth. The plain 2D pocket closes its rows with rings after #3021. These two plans did not.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/motion/tests/pocket_wall_finish_levels.rs` (5 pins). Each pin measures the largest wall scallop at a level. Each pin also checks `verify::crossed_pairs`.\n- `avoid_zigzag_pocket_finishes_walls_and_island`\n- `avoid_auto_pocket_finishes_walls_conventional`\n- `avoid_blended_zigzag_pocket_finishes_walls_without_crossings`\n- `pocket3d_zigzag_levels_finish_the_boss_walls`\n- `pocket3d_auto_levels_finish_the_boss_walls`\n\nRed before the fix (all 5):\n- avoid pocket: outer wall scallop 0.755 mm (0.919 mm with blended turns).\n- 3D pocket: boss wall scallop 2.000 mm at level Z -5.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- `pocket_avoid.rs` put back: the 3 avoid pins fail, and the 2 3D pins pass.\n- `hsm.rs` put back: the 2 3D pins fail, and the 3 avoid pins pass.\n- Fix restored: 5 of 5 pass.\n\nExpected test change: `operations.rs::multiaxis_rough_peels_the_same_ladder_and_poses_its_walls` had `posed <= 20`. The closing ring round the boss poses each ring chord (97 poses). The test now checks that each pose stays within the ball's reach (r 3, tolerance 0.5) of the boss. That is the intent of the old bound.\n\n## Review fixes\n\n1. A restart for a tool that is not center-cutting now stages its helix and checks it against prior feed moves. If it crosses, the restart tries a checked ramp along the pass. It refuses the operation if neither entry is clear.\n   - Pins: `center_cut_law::a_tool_that_is_not_centre_cutting_never_plunges_into_a_pocket_between_passes` and `center_cut_law::a_closing_ring_restart_does_not_cross_the_rows_transition_ramp`. The focused pin requires a successful round pocket with a named ramp fallback and no crossings.\n2. The square and island tests now describe the inset rows and their separate closing rings.\n   - `machining2d::zigzag_fills_a_square_with_rows_and_a_closing_ring_per_level`: four dives, inset row Ys, and the row-plus-ring length.\n   - `machining2d::zigzag_hops_over_islands_and_leaves_them_standing`: fourteen dives. The island distance and chord checks remain.\n3. The KeepDown test now counts the rapid moves that successful planar links avoid. Its gap helper does not see those links.\n   - Pin: `level_links::keep_down_pass_links_stay_at_depth_where_proved_and_say_where_not`. It compares the retract plan and a 0.001 mm stay-down limit. Verification and named-lift checks remain.\n\nThe decision record explains the changed counts and link assertions.\n\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nThis review fix changes no golden file. The branch carries the NC and CL goldens and sample programs from #3130.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `pocket_avoid` blended turns have no crossing-law post as the plain pocket has (`hold_crossings`). The blended pin shows no crossing pair. If a crossing occurs, the post check blocks the program.\n- Rings on the rotary wrap levels: not in this PR. Follow-up: #3168.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3130: base of this stack (`pocket_zigzag::rest_passes`).\n- #3108: touches `machining3d/hsm.rs`, function `rings_tag`. This PR changes `plan_level`. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- `machining2d/mod.rs`: #3136, #3120, #3115, #3112, #3108, #3103, #3059, #2890, #2836, #2822 and #2714 add other lines. This PR adds one re-export line.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/3129-zigzag-closing-rings.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D pockets with \"Do not touch\" and 3D pocket levels cut with Zigzag or Auto now finish the walls and islands with a closing ring.\n\nFixes #3129\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
